.nh
.TH "PB-ENV-NAMES-ACCESS" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-names-access - Show or set whether commands on machines can list ENV names in this workspace


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env names access [on|off] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show, or with on|off set, "Commands on machines can list ENV names" for the active workspace (--workspace, default personal). It is on by default. Off, \fBpb env names\fR on the workspace's machines is refused; \fBpb env run\fR still gives commands their values, so this is a policy for the listing, not a lock. For a team only an owner or admin may change it.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for access

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the setting as JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb env names access
  pb env names access off
  pb env names access on --workspace my-team
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env-names(1)\fP
